  "result": "If I could change just one thing, I'd make curiosity stronger than fear.\n\nFear makes us shut down \u2014 avoid people who are different, cling to what we already believe, assume the worst. Curiosity does the opposite. It makes us ask: *What is that person going through? How does this work? What if I'm wrong? What could we build together?*\n\nI think almost every other big change we want \u2014 kinder communities, better science, healthier politics, more care for the planet \u2014 flows from that one shift. If everyone felt safe enough to stay curious a little longer, we'd listen more, judge less, and solve problems *with* each other instead of *against* each other.\n\nWhat about you? What one change would you pick?",
